---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const entry = await getEntry("home", "page");
if (!entry) {
  throw new Error("Missing home page content");
}

const email = entry.data.footer.email;
const meta = {
  title: "Privacy Policy | Marres",
  description:
    "Read how Marres handles account, billing, company, Google review, analysis, and provider data for its launch service.",
  canonicalUrl: "https://marres.io/privacy",
};
---

<SiteLayout {...meta}>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-content">
      <span class="tag">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Effective 3 September 2026</p>
      <p class="legal-intro">
        This policy explains how Marres Insights Pte Ltd handles data for the
        Marres launch service and this website.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Data we handle</h2>
        <h3>Accounts and access</h3>
        <p>
          We store your email address, password hash, user and tenant records,
          membership role, and server-side session data. We do not store your
          password in plain text.
        </p>
        <h3>Billing</h3>
        <p>
          When billing is enabled, we store Stripe customer, subscription,
          price, checkout, entitlement, and webhook records. Stripe handles the
          hosted payment and billing pages. Marres does not store payment-card
          details.
        </p>
        <h3>Company setup</h3>
        <p>
          You submit one target company and six competitors, with an exact
          Google Maps URL for each. You also select four customer-perception
          domains. We store the submitted names, URLs, selected domains, and the
          source identities confirmed during collection.
        </p>
        <h3>Reviews and analysis</h3>
        <p>
          We store public Google Maps review identifiers, text when available,
          ratings, publication dates, review URLs, and collection details. We
          also store exact evidence excerpts, scores, embeddings, derived
          results, run state, failures, usage, cost, and provider, model,
          prompt, and version records.
        </p>
        <p>
          Apify is configured not to collect reviewer personal data. The Marres
          review record does not include reviewer names or reviewer profiles.
          Public review text can still contain personal information that a
          reviewer chose to publish.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why we use it</h2>
        <p>We use this data to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>create accounts, sessions, tenant access, and billing access;</li>
          <li>collect the requested public reviews;</li>
          <li>produce and display customer-perception analysis;</li>
          <li>
            keep results linked to their source and processing record; and
          </li>
          <li>secure, operate, support, and diagnose the service.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who receives data</h2>
        <p>
          Apify receives the submitted Google Maps URLs and collects the public
          review source data. OpenRouter receives review text, company context,
          and one selected domain for each Luna analysis call. It receives
          validated evidence excerpts for embedding calls. Both OpenRouter
          routes are pinned to OpenAI models without provider fallback.
        </p>
        <p>
          Stripe receives account and billing data needed for its hosted
          checkout and billing pages, then sends Marres subscription and payment
          state. We use service providers only to run these parts of Marres or
          when disclosure is required by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          The public website is hosted on GitHub Pages and loads typefaces from
          Google Fonts. It has no contact form or analytics. Normal web requests
          can give these hosts technical data such as your IP address and
          browser details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Hosting and location</h2>
        <p>
          At the date of this policy, the pre-launch application and PostgreSQL
          database run on a Vultr virtual machine. The application uses a local
          interface, and PostgreSQL uses a private local socket. The public app
          cutover is not complete.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our providers can process data outside Singapore. We do not make a
          data-residency promise. We will update this policy if the production
          data boundary changes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Access, correction, and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Marres does not yet have self-service data export or account deletion.
          Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> to ask for access, correction,
          export, or deletion. We may need to verify that you control the account
          before responding.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We have not adopted fixed public retention periods. We keep account,
          analysis, provider, security, and billing records while needed to run
          and protect the service, support billing, resolve disputes, or meet
          legal duties. Some billing, security, backup, or legal records can
          remain when removal is not permitted or practical.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Contact <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with a privacy question
          or request. We may update this policy when the service or its data handling
          changes. The effective date above shows the current version.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
